[=#platforms]
== Platforms ==

Rudiments is supported on a variety of Linux/Unix systems and Windows.  Building Rudiments on these platforms requires the installation of a compiler toolchain and other bits of optional software.  Instructions follow for many supported platforms.

[=#linux]
=== Linux ===

Rudiments is supported on a variety of Linux platforms including Fedora, !CentOS, !OpenSuSE, Debian, and Ubuntu.

[=#fedora]
==== Fedora ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
dnf -y install gcc-c++ make libedit-devel openssl-devel krb5-devel pcre2-devel libcurl-devel
}}}

The gcc-c++ and make packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the pcre2-devel package.

Note that on older Fedora platforms, the yum package manager is used instead of the dnf package manager.  The syntax for the two is the same though, just replace dnf with yum in the command above.
}}}

[=#centos]
==== !CentOS ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
yum -y install gcc-c++ make libedit-devel openssl-devel krb5-devel pcre2-devel libcurl-devel
}}}

The gcc-c++ and make packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the pcre2-devel package.
}}}

[=#opensuse]
==== !OpenSuSE ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
zypper install gcc-c++ make readline-devel libopenssl-devel krb5-devel pcre2-devel libcurl-devel
}}}

The gcc-c++ and make packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the pcre2-devel package.
}}}

[=#ubuntu]
==== Ubuntu ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
apt-get install g++ make libedit-dev libssl-dev libkrb5-dev libpcre2-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev
}}}

The g++ and make packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the libpcre2-dev package.
}}}

[=#debian]
==== Debian ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
apt-get install g++ make libedit-dev libssl-dev libkrb5-dev libpcre2-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev
}}}

The g++ and make packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the libpcre2-dev package.
}}}

[=#unix]
=== Unix ===

Rudiments is supported on a variety of Unix platforms including !FreeBSD, !NetBSD, !OpenBSD, and Minix.

[=#freebsd]
==== !FreeBSD ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
pkg install clang gmake pkgconf readline openssl pcre2 curl
}}}

The clang and gmake packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the pcre2 package.

Note that on older !FreeBSD platforms:

* The pkgtools package manager is used instead of the pkg package manager and the syntax for the two is the different.  Replace "pkg install" with "pkg_add -r " in the command above.
* Clang is not available, so clang must be replaced with g++.

Kerberos/GSSAPI is installed as part of the base installation.
}}}

[=#netbsd]
==== !NetBSD ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:
 
{{{#!code
pkgin install g++ gmake readline openssl pcre2 curl
}}}

The g++ and gmake packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the pcre2 package.

Kerberos/GSSAPI is installed as part of the base installation.
}}}

[=#openbsd]
==== !OpenBSD ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, add a line to /etc/pkg.conf like:

{{{#!code
installpath = ftp://ftp.usa.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD/5.8/packages/amd64/
}}}

(replacing 5.8 with the version of !OpenBSD that you are using and replacing amd64 with the architecture given by uname -m)

... and execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
pkg_add -r g++ gmake readline heimdal pcre2 curl
}}}

The g++ and gmake packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the pcre2 package.

!OpenSSL is installed as part of the base installation.
}}}

[=#minix]
==== Minix ====

{{{#!blockquote

To install all of the prerequisites at once, execute the following command, as root:

{{{#!code
pkgin install clang binutils gmake readline openssl heimdal pcre2 curl
}}}

The clang, binutils, and gmake packages are required, but the rest are optional and may be omitted as appropriate.  For example, if you don't need PCRE support, then you can omit the pcre2 packages.
}}}

[=#windows]
=== Windows ===

{{{#!blockquote

Rudiments is supported on a variety of Windows platforms.  Building Rudiments on these platforms just requires the installation of a compiler toolchain.

Rudiments can be built using the Microsoft Visual Studio and Visual Studio Express toolchains.  Visual Studio Express can be downloaded for free from [http://www.visualstudio.com Microsoft] and the installer is intuitive.
}}}


